== The go-yaml/yaml Project

* %go-yaml/yaml% is YAML's ^most popular^ implementation
  * Created by ^Gustavo Niemeyer^ in 2014
  * ~^80K Go projects^ on GitHub use go-yaml directly
  * Very heavily used in the ^Kubernetes^ ecosystem
  * Officially %archived April 2025%

+* Two main versions: ^v2^ and ^v3^
  * v3 added ^comment support^

+* ^kubernetes-sigs/yaml forked^
  * Full copies of the v2 and v3 branches' code
  * A few important patches


----
== The yaml/go-yaml Project

* ^yaml/go-yaml^ project started mid-April 2025
  * Blessed fork of %go-yaml/yaml%
  * Formed a solid group of maintainers
  * Davanum Srinivas - ^@dims++^
    * ^UNFORKED^ kubernetes-sigs/yaml on Day 1

+* ^4500 projects have switched^ to yaml/go-yaml
  * Used %in Kubernetes% proper

+* ^Painless transition^ from v2 and v3
  * No new features, only security patches

+* New go-yaml `v4` leads the ^Future of YAML^!

