----
== What if YAML were Fully Programmable?

* Introducing YAMLScript (YS)
* Lets any YAML data be code
* https://yamlscript.org

* %Imagine using Python code as a config language…%

----
== Python Data as Config

# This is a Python program, but it only uses data syntax:

{
    "service": "yaml-api",
    "host": "127.0.0.1",
    "port": 8080,
    "debug": False,
    "workers": 4,
    "allowed_origins": ["https://example.com"],
}

----
== Dynamic Python as Config

# Here we use some code to calculate data values:

{
    "service": "yaml-api",
    "host": ".".join(["127", "0", "0", "1"]),
    "port": 8000 + 80,
    "debug": 1 > 2,
    "workers": 2 * 2,
    "allowed_origins": ["https://example.com"],
}

----
== Dynamic YAML as Config

# Same thing as Python, but the code is YAML:

!ys-0:
service: yaml-api
host:: +[127 0 0 1].join('.')
port:: 8000 + 80
debug:: 1 > 2
workers:: 2 * 2
allowed_origins: [https://example.com]

