== What if YAML had a fully compatible library for every language?

* Fully featured
* Same in every language
  * Same API
  * Same features
  * Same bugs
  * Same fixes

----
== Introducing YAMLStar

* https://yamlstar.org
  * A YAML framework for 32 programming languages (so far!)

* Has a CLI called "yaml", very similar to the "go-yaml" CLI
  $ go-yaml -J <<<'a: [ok, 1, 2.3, true, null]'
  $ yaml    -J <<<'a: [ok, 1, 2.3, true, null]'

* YAMLStar works the same in every language
  * Same API, same features, same bugs, same fixes

* YAMLStar has a Plugin System!
  * Same plugins for all languages
  * ^Most plugins are shared with go-yaml!!^

----
== YAMLStar -> New YAML Spec!

* YAML 1.2 dates to 2009
  * Many YAMLs are still at 1.1

* YAMLStar is how we get to %YAML 1.3% (or 2.0)!
  * Working ^implementations in every language^ *before* release!
  * Plugins let us ^experiment with new ideas^ in YAML 1.2…
    before deciding what goes into the next YAML spec!

* YAMLStar has plugins
  * Plugins let us try new things
  * go-yaml has many of the same plugins!

* ^Popular new ideas become part of the next spec^
  * Implementations in every language
  * Before the spec is published!
  * YAMLStar and %go-yaml plugins are the key to YAML 1.3!%

