== What if YAML had a Schema Language?

  https://yamlschema.org

* A superset of JSON Schema
* Concise and easy to understand
* ysd tool converts .ysd.yaml <-> .schema.json
* Full semantic round-tripping

$ cat person.schema.json
$ ysd person.schema.json
$ ysd person.schema.json | ysd -
$ ysd -R person.schema.json

----
== What if YAML supported tab indentation?

$ cat tabs.yaml
$ sed 's/\t/=>/g' tabs.yaml

$ yaml    -J --plugin=tab-indent tabs.yaml
$ go-yaml -J --plugin=tab-indent tabs.yaml

$ vim tabs.go
$ go run tabs.go

----
== The %Dump%/%Load% Stack (How a YAML really works)
== https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/#31-processes

              %Loader%             Data State              %Dumper%
         ===========================================================
                                (YAML Input)
              Reader                                     Writer
                           (YAML Character Stream)
             Scanner
                             (YAML Token Stream)
              `Parser`                                     Emitter
                             ^(YAML Event Stream)^
            `Composer`                                     Serializer
                               (YAML Node Tree)
            `Resolver`                                     Desolver
                        ^(Tagged Representation Graph)^
         `Constructor`                                     Representer
                            (Native Data Objects)

----
== The YAML Load Stack in Action

* The YAMLStar `yaml` CLI has a `-d` debug option

$ yaml -d <<<'a: [b, 3, true]'

* The go-yaml CLI also has stack inspection options

* ^Understanding the Stack is the key to really understanding YAML^

----
== What if you could write plugins in YAML?

* %YAML is Go%. Should be easy!

* The `YAML-Parser` plugin API
  * Swap out entire parsers for go-yaml

* ^Current parser plugins^
  go-yaml       - Native Go parser (go-yaml & YAMLStar default)
  reference     - YAML reference grammar parser
  snakeyaml     - Java's SnakeYAML Engine parser
  rapidyaml     - C++ RapidYAML parser
  json-comments - YAML parser supporting C-style comments
  %toml          - Parse TOML to YAML events%
  ^csv           - Parse CSV/TSV to YAML events^

----
== yamlstar-plugin-parser-csv

* A CSV frontend for go-yaml or YAMLStar
* Written in YAMLScript!

* https://github.com/yamlstar/yamlstar-plugin-parser-csv/blob/main/src/csv_parser/core.ys

$ cat data.csv

$ make cli PLUGIN-PACKAGE=github.com/yamlstar/yamlstar-plugin-parser-csv/goyaml@v0.1.0

$ go-yaml -J --plugin=yaml-parser=csv data.csv

$ go-yaml -e --plugin=yaml-parser=csv data.csv

----
== YAML Plugin APIs

* ^Alias-Data^      - Powerful aliasing
* Allowed-Bugs    - Choose which fixed bugs to retain
* Comment-Model   - Better comment loading
* ^Error-Format^    - Custom error formatting
* %Function-Tag%    - Define your own function calls: `!load vars: vars.yaml`
* L10N-Keys       - YAML keys in French or Chinese
* ^Loader-Limits^   - Custom resource limits
* Merge-Key       - Custom `<<` merge key behavior
* Multi-Tag       - Multiple tags `!!foo;bar`
* Stream-Tag      - `!!yaml:helm.sh/v4`
* ^Tab-Indent^      - Use tabs for YAML indentation
* YAML-Format     - Completely custom YAML formatting
* ^YAML-Parser^     - Use an alternate YAML parser
* YAML-Rules      - Use `oui` and `non` for `true` and `false`
* YAML-Schema     - Schema validation and association

