== What if YAML aliases (*foo) could reference anything?

* Not just anchors
* Environment variables
* Program vars
* Anything you want

---- skip
== Alias-Data Plugin

* Ordinary aliases resolve anchors in the current document
* Alias-Data adds values from:
  * Inline configuration, files and the environment
  * Anchors from previous documents in the stream
* It is opt-in: ordinary YAML behavior stays unchanged

---- skip
== Alias-Data Plugin

  External values:
$ vim -O alias-data.yaml alias-data-config.yaml
$ SPEAKER=Ingy yaml --config=alias-data-config.yaml -y alias-data.yaml

  The same configuration in go-yaml:
$ make -C repos/go-yaml cli
$ SPEAKER=Ingy go-yaml --config=alias-data-config.yaml -y alias-data.yaml

---- skip
== Alias-Data Plugin

  An anchor in one document, an alias in the next:
$ vim alias-stream.yaml

  Ordinary YAML rejects the cross-document alias:
$ go-yaml -y alias-stream.yaml

  Alias-Data retains the anchor for the stream:
$ go-yaml --plugin=alias-data -y alias-stream.yaml

